**What happens:** `tasks.quickAdd` always returns 404.

**Why:** in `packages/todoist/endpoints/tasks.ts:168-180`:

```ts
const result = await makeTodoistRequest<...>(
	'quick/add', ctx.key, { method: 'POST', body: input },
);
```

The plugin's client base is `https://api.todoist.com/api/v1` (`packages/todoist/client.ts:15`), and `quick/add` is the old REST v2 path. In the v1 API the natural-language quick add lives at `POST /tasks/quick` ([Todoist API docs](https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1)), so this call hits a route that no longer exists.

**Fix:** change the endpoint path to `'tasks/quick'`. No other changes needed.

**What happens:** calling `contacts.attachToCompany` returns success but the company is never attached to the contact. Intercom silently ignores the unknown field.

**Why:** `attachToCompany` in `packages/intercom/endpoints/contacts.ts:220-231` destructures `contact_id` and sends the rest as the body:

```ts
const { contact_id, ...body } = input;
const result = await makeIntercomRequest<...>(
	`contacts/${contact_id}/companies`, ctx.key,
	{ method: 'POST', body },
);
```

Since the input schema is `{ contact_id, company_id }`, this sends `{ company_id: "..." }`. Per [Intercom's docs](https://developers.intercom.com/docs/references/rest-api/api.intercom.io/companies/attachcontacttoacompany), the endpoint expects a single required field, `id`:

```json
{ "id": "<company_id>" }
```

So the request body field doesn't match what the API reads.

**Fix:** send the field the API expects:

```ts
{ method: 'POST', body: { id: input.company_id } }
```

